# M7.1 acceptance: the Preferences dialog, driven by keyboard only.
#
# Run from the worktree root with an isolated HOME (so wxConfig and the logs
# never touch the real home), an unreachable session bus (so the run never
# reaches the user's keyring and the key store is reliably unavailable), and
# the fake sidecar (so "Test key" never touches the network):
#
#   H=$(mktemp -d)
#   O=<repo>/.verify/m7.1/<impl|review|tester>
#   READER_SIDECAR_CMD="$PWD/tests/acceptance/m7.1-fake-sidecar.sh" \
#     scripts/shot.sh -o "$O" -s tests/acceptance/m7.1.steps -- \
#     env HOME="$H" DBUS_SESSION_BUS_ADDRESS=unix:path=/nonexistent \
#     ./build/app/agentic-reader
#   grep -rl claude-test-model "$H"            # must list the wxConfig file
#   tests/acceptance/m7.1-grep.sh "$H" "$O"    # must exit 0
#
# The first grep proves the settings were written, so the second grep is not
# vacuous. Pass: shot.sh exits 0, every shot matches its comment, both greps
# behave as stated.
#
# The fake sidecar (tests/acceptance/m7.1-fake-sidecar.sh) answers `prompt`
# with error kind `auth` when ANTHROPIC_API_KEY reached it, `internal` when
# it did not, `no_project` for a new_chat before open_project, and
# `unknown_chat` for a prompt to a chat it never started.
#
# Fake key, never a real one: sk-ant-test-FAKEKEY0123456789
#
# Assumptions the steps rely on (the spec is silent):
#   - The menu bar reads File, Edit, Help. "&Edit" has mnemonic E and its
#     Preferences item (wxID_PREFERENCES) has mnemonic P.
#   - The dialog opens with keyboard focus in the API key field.
#   - Tab order follows spec item 3: key field, Show, Test key, model field,
#     dev checkbox. Show is a check box or toggle button, so Space flips it.
#   - The key field stays editable when the key store is unavailable, so Show
#     and Test key still work. The key is just not saved.
#   - "Test key" reports its result inside the dialog (a status line), not in
#     a separate message box.
#   - OK is the default button: Return in the model field accepts the dialog.
#     OK saves the model and the dev flag. With no key store it saves no key
#     and opens no extra message box (the dialog already showed why).
#   - Escape cancels the dialog.
wait 2

# Main window with the menu bar open on Edit: "Edit" sits between "File" and
# "Help", and its menu shows a "Preferences" item.
key alt+e
wait 1
shot edit-menu

key p
wait 2

# The Preferences dialog is open over the main window and shows:
#   - an empty API key field with a "Show" toggle (off) and a "Test key" button,
#   - an empty model field (empty means the SDK default),
#   - an unchecked "Use my local Claude Code login (developer)" check box with
#     a one-line warning that it is for personal use only,
#   - OK and Cancel buttons.
# Key store unavailable (expected for this run): a visible message says the
# key cannot be stored securely and why (for example, no secret service), and
# nothing suggests a plain-text fallback.
# Key store available (a run with a working secret service): no such message.
shot dialog-open

type sk-ant-test-FAKEKEY0123456789
wait 1

# The key field holds 29 mask characters (dots or asterisks). No part of
# "sk-ant-test-FAKEKEY0123456789" is readable anywhere on screen.
shot key-masked

# Tab to Show and turn it on.
key Tab
key space
wait 1

# Show is on and the key field shows the plain text
# "sk-ant-test-FAKEKEY0123456789". Everything else is unchanged.
shot key-shown

# Tab to Test key and press it. The fake sidecar answers with an auth error.
key Tab
key space
wait 4

# The dialog reports that the test failed with error kind "auth" (the word
# "auth" or an equivalent invalid-key message naming the auth kind is
# visible). It must not report "internal" (the key did not reach the sidecar),
# "no_project" or "unknown_chat" (the wrong message order), and must not say
# OK. The status line does not contain the key. The dialog is still open.
shot test-key-auth

# Tab to the model field and type a model, then Tab to the dev check box and
# check it.
key Tab
type claude-test-model
key Tab
key space
wait 1

# The model field reads "claude-test-model" and the dev check box is checked.
# Its one-line personal-use warning is still visible. The key field and the
# Test key result are unchanged.
shot model-and-dev

# Back to the model field and press Return to accept the dialog (OK).
key shift+Tab
key Return
wait 2

# The dialog is closed. The main window is back with no other dialog or
# message box open.
shot saved

# Reopen Preferences the same way.
key alt+e
wait 1
key p
wait 2

# The reopened dialog shows the saved settings: model "claude-test-model" and
# the dev check box checked.
# Key store unavailable (expected for this run): the key field is empty
# because nothing stored the key, and the unavailable message shows again.
# Key store available: the key field holds the saved key, masked (29 mask
# characters), and Show is off.
shot reopened

# Cancel. The app keeps running.
key Escape
wait 1

# The dialog is closed and the main window is back.
shot closed
